":"G3708G = a Meaning of","unique_id":"G1492H","headword":"ὁράω","transliteration":"horaō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to see: see","definition_en":"ὁράω, -ῶ, \n [in LXX chiefly for ראה, also for חזה, etc. ;] in \"durative\" sense (hence aor. act., εἶδον, pass., ὤφθην, fut., ὄψομαι, from different roots; see M, Pr., 110f.), to see (in colloq. even the present is rare, its place being generally taken by θεωρέω, see BL, §24). \n__1. Of bodily vision, to see, perceive, behold: absol., Mrk.6:38, al.; ἔρχου καὶ ἴδε, Jhn.1:46, al.; before ὅτι, Mrk.2:16, al.; with accusative, Mat.2:2, Mrk.1:10 16:7, Gal.1:19, al.; θεόν, Jhn.1:18, 1Jn.4:20, al. \n __2. to see with the mind, perceive, discern: absol, Rom.15:21; with accusative of thing(s), Mat.9:2 27:54, Act.8:23, Col.2:18, al. \n __3. to see, take heed, beware: ὅρα μή, with aor. subjc., Mat.8:4 18:10, Mrk.1:44, 1Th.5:15; id., sc. μὴ ποήσῃς, Rev.19:10 22:9 (Bl., §81, 1); before imperat. Mat.9:30 16:6, Mrk.8:15 \n __4. to experience: τ. θάνατον, Luk.2:26, Heb.11:5; ζωήν, Jhn.3:36; τ. διαφθοράν, Act.2:27. \n __5. to visit: with accusative of person(s), Luk.8:20, Jhn.12:21, Rom.1:11, al.; with accusative loc, Act.19:21. \n __6. to see to, care for: Mat.27:4, Act.18:15 (cf. ἀφ-, καθ-, προ-, συν-οράω). \n SYN.: see: βλέπω. (AS)","source_line":3824},{"source_id":"G3708","disambiguated_id":"G3708H = a Meaning of","unique_id":"G1492H","headword":"ὁράω","transliteration":"horaō","lexical_morphology":"G:V","gloss_en":"to see: appear","definition_en":"ὁράω, -ῶ, \n [in LXX chiefly for ראה, also for חזה, etc. ;] in \"durative\" sense (hence aor. act., εἶδον, pass., ὤφθην, fut., ὄψομαι, from different roots; see M, Pr., 110f.), to see (in colloq. even the present is rare, its place being generally taken by θεωρέω, see BL, §24). \n__1. Of bodily vision, to see, perceive, behold: absol., Mrk.6:38, al.; ἔρχου καὶ ἴδε, Jhn.1:46, al.; before ὅτι, Mrk.2:16, al.; with accusative, Mat.2:2, Mrk.1:10 16:7, Gal.1:19, al.; θεόν, Jhn.1:18, 1Jn.4:20, al. \n __2. to see with the mind, perceive, discern: absol, Rom.15:21; with accusative of thing(s), Mat.9:2 27:54, Act.8:23, Col.2:18, al. \n __3. to see, take heed, beware: ὅρα μή, with aor. subjc., Mat.8:4 18:10, Mrk.1:44, 1Th.5:15; id., sc. μὴ ποήσῃς, Rev.19:10 22:9 (Bl., §81, 1); before imperat. Mat.9:30 16:6, Mrk.8:15 \n __4. to experience: τ. θάνατον, Luk.2:26, Heb.11:5; ζωήν, Jhn.3:36; τ. διαφθοράν, Act.2:27. \n __5. to visit: with accusative of person(s), Luk.8:20, Jhn.12:21, Rom.1:11, al.; with accusative loc, Act.19:21. \n __6. to see to, care for: Mat.27:4, Act.18:15 (cf. ἀφ-, καθ-, προ-, συν-οράω). \n SYN.: see: βλέπω. (AS)","source_line":3825}],"occurrence_count":476,"observed_portuguese_glosses":[{"gloss":"viu","count":73},{"gloss":"vendo","count":53},{"gloss":"vi","count":48},{"gloss":"ver","count":40},{"gloss":"viram","count":38},{"gloss":"visto","count":30},{"gloss":"sabendo","count":20},{"gloss":"vimos","count":14},{"gloss":"vereis","count":13},{"gloss":"verão","count":10},{"gloss":"olhei","count":10},{"gloss":"quando","count":9},{"gloss":"vede","count":9},{"gloss":"virdes","count":8},{"gloss":"apareceu","count":8},{"gloss":"vê","count":8},{"gloss":"viste","count":8},{"gloss":"vejam","count":7},{"gloss":"olhai","count":7},{"gloss":"vistes","count":6},{"gloss":"olha","count":5},{"gloss":"vejamos","count":5},{"gloss":"apareceram","count":3},{"gloss":"verás","count":3},{"gloss":"verá","count":3},{"gloss":"percebereis","count":2},{"gloss":"vejo","count":2},{"gloss":"veja","count":2},{"gloss":"vedes","count":2},{"gloss":"verei","count":2}]},"G3787":{"id":"G3787","source":"TBESG","entries":[{"source_id":"G3787","disambiguated_id":"G3787 =","unique_id":"G3787","headword":"ὀφθαλμοδουλεία","transliteration":"ophthalmodouleia","lexical_morphology":"G:N-F","gloss_en":"eye-service","definition_en":"ὀφθαλμο-δουλία (Rec. -εία), -ας, ἡ \n (ὀφθαλμός, δοῦλος), \neye-service: Eph.6:6, Col.3:22 (not found elsewhere).†\n (AS)","source_line":3905}],"occurrenc